{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router provides flexible and highly customizable primitives that can be composed to support common internationalization (i18n) routing patterns, such as "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"optional path parameters"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"route rewriting"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type-safe params"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This enables clean, SEO-friendly URLs, flexible locale handling, and seamless integration with i18n libraries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix-based and optional-locale routing"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced routing patterns for i18n"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language navigation and switching"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SEO considerations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type safety"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Integration patterns with i18n libraries (Paraglide)"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"i18n-with-optional-path-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"i18n with Optional Path Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern relies exclusively on TanStack Router features. It is suitable when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want full control over translations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You already manage translations manually"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not need automatic locale detection"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional path parameters are ideal for implementing locale-aware routing without duplicating routes."}]},{"type":"code","value":"/{-$locale}/about"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This single route matches:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (default locale)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/en/about"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/fr/about"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/es/about"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"prefix-based-i18n","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix-based i18n"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en'\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us' },\n    fr: { title: 'À Propos' },\n    es: { title: 'Acerca de' },\n  }\n\n  return <h1>{content[currentLocale].title}</h1>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"complex-routing-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complex Routing Patterns"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n\n    if (params.locale && !validLocales.includes(params.locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"language-switching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language Switching"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Link\n  to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n  params={(prev) => ({\n    ...prev,\n    locale: prev.locale === 'en' ? undefined : 'fr',\n  })}\n>\n  Français\n</Link>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-safe-locales","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-safe Locales"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\nfunction isLocale(value?: string): value is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(value as Locale)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"i18n-library-integration-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"i18n Library Integration Patterns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"library-agnostic"}]},{"type":"text","value":". You can integrate any i18n solution by mapping locale state to routing behavior."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Below is a recommended pattern using "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paraglide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-side-i18n-with-a-library-tanstack-router","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side i18n with a Library (TanStack Router)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern combines TanStack Router with a client-side i18n library. It is suitable when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want type-safe translations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want localized URLs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not need server-side rendering"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tanstack-router-paraglide-client-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router + Paraglide (Client-only)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paraglide provides type-safe translations, locale detection, and URL localization that pair naturally with TanStack Router."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub example:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"project-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project Setup"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npx @inlang/paraglide-js@latest init","lang":"bash"},{"type":"code","value":"import { paraglideVitePlugin } from '@inlang/paraglide-js'\n\nparaglideVitePlugin({\n  project: './project.inlang',\n  outdir: './app/paraglide',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"url-localization-via-router-rewrite","children":[{"type":"text","value":"URL Localization via Router Rewrite"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The router's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rewrite"},{"type":"text","value":" option enables bidirectional URL transformation, perfect for locale prefixes. For comprehensive documentation on URL rewrites including advanced patterns, see the "},{"type":"link","href":"./url-rewrites.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"URL Rewrites guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { deLocalizeUrl, localizeUrl } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  rewrite: {\n    input: ({ url }) => deLocalizeUrl(url),\n    output: ({ url }) => localizeUrl(url),\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-side-i18n-tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-side i18n (TanStack Start)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern integrates i18n at the routing and server layers. It is suitable when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You use TanStack Start"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You need SSR or streaming"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want locale-aware redirects and metadata"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tanstack-start-paraglide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start + Paraglide"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub example:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server-middleware-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Middleware (SSR)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { paraglideMiddleware } from './paraglide/server'\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(req: Request) {\n    return paraglideMiddleware(req, () => handler.fetch(req))\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"html-language-attribute","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML Language Attribute"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getLocale } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n;<html lang={getLocale()} />","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"offline-safe-redirects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Offline-safe Redirects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For offline or client-only environments:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { shouldRedirect } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n\nbeforeLoad: async () => {\n  const decision = await shouldRedirect({ url: window.location.href })\n  if (decision.redirectUrl) {\n    throw redirect({ href: decision.redirectUrl.href })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-safe-translated-pathnames","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type-safe Translated Pathnames"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To ensure every route has translations, you can derive translated pathnames directly from the TanStack Router route tree."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { FileRoutesByTo } from '../routeTree.gen'\nimport { Locale } from '@/paraglide/runtime'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guarantees:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No missing translations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full type safety"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiler feedback for routing mistakes"}]}]}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prerendering-localized-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerendering Localized Routes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { localizeHref } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nexport const prerenderRoutes = ['/', '/about'].map((path) => ({\n  path: localizeHref(path),\n  prerender: { enabled: true },\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"additional-i18n-integration-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional i18n Integration Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"intlayer-tanstack-start-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intlayer (TanStack Start integration)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"use-intl-tanstack-start-integration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"use-intl (TanStack Start integration)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"i18n-with-optional-path-parameters","text":"i18n with Optional Path Parameters","level":2},{"id":"prefix-based-i18n","text":"Prefix-based i18n","level":3},{"id":"complex-routing-patterns","text":"Complex Routing Patterns","level":3},{"id":"language-switching","text":"Language Switching","level":3},{"id":"type-safe-locales","text":"Type-safe Locales","level":3},{"id":"i18n-library-integration-patterns","text":"i18n Library Integration Patterns","level":2},{"id":"client-side-i18n-with-a-library-tanstack-router","text":"Client-side i18n with a Library (TanStack Router)","level":2},{"id":"tanstack-router-paraglide-client-only","text":"TanStack Router + Paraglide (Client-only)","level":3},{"id":"project-setup","text":"Project Setup","level":3},{"id":"url-localization-via-router-rewrite","text":"URL Localization via Router Rewrite","level":3},{"id":"server-side-i18n-tanstack-start","text":"Server-side i18n (TanStack Start)","level":2},{"id":"tanstack-start-paraglide","text":"TanStack Start + Paraglide","level":3},{"id":"server-middleware-ssr","text":"Server Middleware (SSR)","level":3},{"id":"html-language-attribute","text":"HTML Language Attribute","level":3},{"id":"offline-safe-redirects","text":"Offline-safe Redirects","level":2},{"id":"type-safe-translated-pathnames","text":"Type-safe Translated Pathnames","level":2},{"id":"prerendering-localized-routes","text":"Prerendering Localized Routes","level":2},{"id":"additional-i18n-integration-patterns","text":"Additional i18n Integration Patterns","level":2},{"id":"intlayer-tanstack-start-integration","text":"Intlayer (TanStack Start integration)","level":3},{"id":"use-intl-tanstack-start-integration","text":"use-intl (TanStack Start integration)","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Router provides flexible and highly customizable primitives that can be composed to support common internationalization (i18n) routing patterns, such as **optional path parameters**, **route rewriting**, and **type-safe params**. This enables clean, SEO-friendly URLs, flexible locale handling, and seamless integration with i18n libraries.\n\nThis guide covers:\n\n- Prefix-based and optional-locale routing\n- Advanced routing patterns for i18n\n- Language navigation and switching\n- SEO considerations\n- Type safety\n- Integration patterns with i18n libraries (Paraglide)\n\n---\n\n## i18n with Optional Path Parameters\n\nThis pattern relies exclusively on TanStack Router features. It is suitable when:\n\n- You want full control over translations\n- You already manage translations manually\n- You do not need automatic locale detection\n\nOptional path parameters are ideal for implementing locale-aware routing without duplicating routes.\n\n```\n/{-$locale}/about\n```\n\nThis single route matches:\n\n- `/about` (default locale)\n- `/en/about`\n- `/fr/about`\n- `/es/about`\n\n### Prefix-based i18n\n\n```tsx\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en'\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us' },\n    fr: { title: 'À Propos' },\n    es: { title: 'Acerca de' },\n  }\n\n  return <h1>{content[currentLocale].title}</h1>\n}\n```\n\n### Complex Routing Patterns\n\n```tsx\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n\n    if (params.locale && !validLocales.includes(params.locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Language Switching\n\n```tsx\n<Link\n  to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n  params={(prev) => ({\n    ...prev,\n    locale: prev.locale === 'en' ? undefined : 'fr',\n  })}\n>\n  Français\n</Link>\n```\n\n### Type-safe Locales\n\n```ts\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\nfunction isLocale(value?: string): value is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(value as Locale)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## i18n Library Integration Patterns\n\nTanStack Router is **library-agnostic**. You can integrate any i18n solution by mapping locale state to routing behavior.\n\nBelow is a recommended pattern using **Paraglide**.\n\n---\n\n## Client-side i18n with a Library (TanStack Router)\n\nThis pattern combines TanStack Router with a client-side i18n library. It is suitable when:\n\n- You want type-safe translations\n- You want localized URLs\n- You do not need server-side rendering\n\n### TanStack Router + Paraglide (Client-only)\n\nParaglide provides type-safe translations, locale detection, and URL localization that pair naturally with TanStack Router.\n\n**GitHub example:**\n[https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide)\n\n### Project Setup\n\n```bash\nnpx @inlang/paraglide-js@latest init\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { paraglideVitePlugin } from '@inlang/paraglide-js'\n\nparaglideVitePlugin({\n  project: './project.inlang',\n  outdir: './app/paraglide',\n})\n```\n\n### URL Localization via Router Rewrite\n\nThe router's `rewrite` option enables bidirectional URL transformation, perfect for locale prefixes. For comprehensive documentation on URL rewrites including advanced patterns, see the [URL Rewrites guide](./url-rewrites.md).\n\n```ts\nimport { deLocalizeUrl, localizeUrl } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  rewrite: {\n    input: ({ url }) => deLocalizeUrl(url),\n    output: ({ url }) => localizeUrl(url),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Server-side i18n (TanStack Start)\n\nThis pattern integrates i18n at the routing and server layers. It is suitable when:\n\n- You use TanStack Start\n- You need SSR or streaming\n- You want locale-aware redirects and metadata\n\n### TanStack Start + Paraglide\n\n**GitHub example:**\n[https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide)\n\n### Server Middleware (SSR)\n\n```ts\nimport { paraglideMiddleware } from './paraglide/server'\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(req: Request) {\n    return paraglideMiddleware(req, () => handler.fetch(req))\n  },\n}\n```\n\n### HTML Language Attribute\n\n```tsx\nimport { getLocale } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n;<html lang={getLocale()} />\n```\n\n---\n\n## Offline-safe Redirects\n\nFor offline or client-only environments:\n\n```ts\nimport { shouldRedirect } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n\nbeforeLoad: async () => {\n  const decision = await shouldRedirect({ url: window.location.href })\n  if (decision.redirectUrl) {\n    throw redirect({ href: decision.redirectUrl.href })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Type-safe Translated Pathnames\n\nTo ensure every route has translations, you can derive translated pathnames directly from the TanStack Router route tree.\n\n```ts\nimport { FileRoutesByTo } from '../routeTree.gen'\nimport { Locale } from '@/paraglide/runtime'\n```\n\nThis guarantees:\n\n- No missing translations\n- Full type safety\n- Compiler feedback for routing mistakes\n\n---\n\n## Prerendering Localized Routes\n\n```ts\nimport { localizeHref } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nexport const prerenderRoutes = ['/', '/about'].map((path) => ({\n  path: localizeHref(path),\n  prerender: { enabled: true },\n}))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Additional i18n Integration Patterns\n\n### Intlayer (TanStack Start integration)\n\n[https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start](https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start)\n\n### use-intl (TanStack Start integration)\n\n[https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/](https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Internationalization (i18n)\n---\n\nTanStack Router provides flexible and highly customizable primitives that can be composed to support common internationalization (i18n) routing patterns, such as **optional path parameters**, **route rewriting**, and **type-safe params**. This enables clean, SEO-friendly URLs, flexible locale handling, and seamless integration with i18n libraries.\n\nThis guide covers:\n\n- Prefix-based and optional-locale routing\n- Advanced routing patterns for i18n\n- Language navigation and switching\n- SEO considerations\n- Type safety\n- Integration patterns with i18n libraries (Paraglide)\n\n---\n\n## i18n with Optional Path Parameters\n\nThis pattern relies exclusively on TanStack Router features. It is suitable when:\n\n- You want full control over translations\n- You already manage translations manually\n- You do not need automatic locale detection\n\nOptional path parameters are ideal for implementing locale-aware routing without duplicating routes.\n\n```\n/{-$locale}/about\n```\n\nThis single route matches:\n\n- `/about` (default locale)\n- `/en/about`\n- `/fr/about`\n- `/es/about`\n\n### Prefix-based i18n\n\n```tsx\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en'\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us' },\n    fr: { title: 'À Propos' },\n    es: { title: 'Acerca de' },\n  }\n\n  return <h1>{content[currentLocale].title}</h1>\n}\n```\n\n### Complex Routing Patterns\n\n```tsx\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n\n    if (params.locale && !validLocales.includes(params.locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Language Switching\n\n```tsx\n<Link\n  to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n  params={(prev) => ({\n    ...prev,\n    locale: prev.locale === 'en' ? undefined : 'fr',\n  })}\n>\n  Français\n</Link>\n```\n\n### Type-safe Locales\n\n```ts\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\nfunction isLocale(value?: string): value is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(value as Locale)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## i18n Library Integration Patterns\n\nTanStack Router is **library-agnostic**. You can integrate any i18n solution by mapping locale state to routing behavior.\n\nBelow is a recommended pattern using **Paraglide**.\n\n---\n\n## Client-side i18n with a Library (TanStack Router)\n\nThis pattern combines TanStack Router with a client-side i18n library. It is suitable when:\n\n- You want type-safe translations\n- You want localized URLs\n- You do not need server-side rendering\n\n### TanStack Router + Paraglide (Client-only)\n\nParaglide provides type-safe translations, locale detection, and URL localization that pair naturally with TanStack Router.\n\n**GitHub example:**\n[https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/i18n-paraglide)\n\n### Project Setup\n\n```bash\nnpx @inlang/paraglide-js@latest init\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { paraglideVitePlugin } from '@inlang/paraglide-js'\n\nparaglideVitePlugin({\n  project: './project.inlang',\n  outdir: './app/paraglide',\n})\n```\n\n### URL Localization via Router Rewrite\n\nThe router's `rewrite` option enables bidirectional URL transformation, perfect for locale prefixes. For comprehensive documentation on URL rewrites including advanced patterns, see the [URL Rewrites guide](./url-rewrites.md).\n\n```ts\nimport { deLocalizeUrl, localizeUrl } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  rewrite: {\n    input: ({ url }) => deLocalizeUrl(url),\n    output: ({ url }) => localizeUrl(url),\n  },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Server-side i18n (TanStack Start)\n\nThis pattern integrates i18n at the routing and server layers. It is suitable when:\n\n- You use TanStack Start\n- You need SSR or streaming\n- You want locale-aware redirects and metadata\n\n### TanStack Start + Paraglide\n\n**GitHub example:**\n[https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide](https://github.com/TanStack/router/tree/main/examples/react/start-i18n-paraglide)\n\n### Server Middleware (SSR)\n\n```ts\nimport { paraglideMiddleware } from './paraglide/server'\n\nexport default {\n  fetch(req: Request) {\n    return paraglideMiddleware(req, () => handler.fetch(req))\n  },\n}\n```\n\n### HTML Language Attribute\n\n```tsx\nimport { getLocale } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n;<html lang={getLocale()} />\n```\n\n---\n\n## Offline-safe Redirects\n\nFor offline or client-only environments:\n\n```ts\nimport { shouldRedirect } from '../paraglide/runtime'\n\nbeforeLoad: async () => {\n  const decision = await shouldRedirect({ url: window.location.href })\n  if (decision.redirectUrl) {\n    throw redirect({ href: decision.redirectUrl.href })\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Type-safe Translated Pathnames\n\nTo ensure every route has translations, you can derive translated pathnames directly from the TanStack Router route tree.\n\n```ts\nimport { FileRoutesByTo } from '../routeTree.gen'\nimport { Locale } from '@/paraglide/runtime'\n```\n\nThis guarantees:\n\n- No missing translations\n- Full type safety\n- Compiler feedback for routing mistakes\n\n---\n\n## Prerendering Localized Routes\n\n```ts\nimport { localizeHref } from './paraglide/runtime'\n\nexport const prerenderRoutes = ['/', '/about'].map((path) => ({\n  path: localizeHref(path),\n  prerender: { enabled: true },\n}))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Additional i18n Integration Patterns\n\n### Intlayer (TanStack Start integration)\n\n[https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start](https://intlayer.org/doc/environment/tanstack-start)\n\n### use-intl (TanStack Start integration)\n\n[https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/](https://nikuscs.com/blog/13-tanstackstart-i18n/)\n"}
